republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P8 (S39): "go beyond (have more than)" is taken as to want to get a greater share of gain or advantage than others, as in overreaching in P8 P9 and as to want to exceed the correct measure of one's art, doing more or other than another skilled practitioner would where exceeds_like is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r2.sense1)
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {just, unjust}; bad = ∅, exceeds_like = ∅, exceeds_like_2 = {unjust}, exceeds_unlike = {just, unjust}, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, like_evil_ignorant = ∅, like_wise_good = {just, unjust}, wise = ∅
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P8 (S39): "go beyond (have more than)" is taken as to want to get a greater share of gain or advantage than others, as in overreaching in P8 P9 and as to want to exceed the correct measure of one's art compared with the unskilled where exceeds_unlike is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r2.sense2)
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {just, unjust}; bad = ∅, exceeds_like = {unjust}, exceeds_unlike = ∅, exceeds_unlike_2 = {just, unjust}, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, like_evil_ignorant = ∅, like_wise_good = ∅, wise = ∅
